    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Approximately 250 million children under age 5 in low- to middle-income countries (LMICs)\r\nface developmental delays. The problem of early childhood developmental delays is pronounced\r\nin rural China, with up to 86% of children aged 0-3 experiencing delays in at least one of 4\r\ndomains in cognitive, language, motor, and social-emotional development. Parenting programs\r\nin LMICs have shown promise in enhancing early childhood cognitive, language, and motor skill\r\ndevelopment but have inconsistent results for social-emotional development. The study aims to\r\ndetermine whether these interventions significantly improve children's social-emotional\r\noutcomes and if caregiver mental health and parental investment mediate these effects. The\r\nsample comprised 2,554 caregiver-child dyads from 3 randomized controlled trials conducted in\r\nrural China in the period between 2015 and 2022. Results indicated marginal benefits for male\r\nchildren in the lowest family asset quartile; however, no significant overall improvement in\r\nsocial-emotional outcomes was observed. Additionally, parental investment in psychosocial\r\nstimulation of young children significantly mediated these effects, especially for male children.\r\nCaregiver’s mental health did not show significant changes post-intervention and did not mediate\r\nthe outcomes. The findings highlight the heterogeneous impact of parenting interventions. This\r\nstudy also underscores the importance of investing in early childhood development through\r\ntailored interventions that consider gender and socioeconomic disparities.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Zhang, J. (2024). The Mediating Role of Caregiver Mental Health and Parental Investment on EarlyChildhood Social-Emotional Development Outcomes: Evidence from Rural China. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/ks516zw7792. https://doi.org/10.25740/ks516zw7792.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
